course: dictionary
lesson: 640
title: Backup: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. The word backup is a good example. «A backup is an extra copy kept somewhere else, such as a cloud service or an external drive.» Here backup means a spare copy of your files, kept safe in case the first copy is lost.
explain: The same word can also mean extra help. In stories, police «call for backup» when a situation is too big for the officers already there. Here backup means more people who join in to support the ones who are already working.
explain: Backup can also mean a plan kept ready. A «backup plan» is what you use if the first plan fails. To check your meaning, put it into the sentence in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Backup is a noun (a backup, backups) and an adjective (backup plan).
fact: «Backup» means an extra copy of computer files, kept safe in case the first copy is lost.
fact: «Backup» can also mean extra help, or something kept ready in case the first plan fails.
fact: «Back up» is a phrase used as a verb: to back up your files means to copy them, and to back someone up means to support them.
fact: Keep important things in at least two places, because a single copy can be lost.
exercise: «A backup is an extra copy kept somewhere else.» What does backup mean here? | A player who sits on the bench | A jam of cars on the motorway | A loud noise in the night | *An extra copy of files, kept safe
exercise: The police «called for backup» at the scene. What does backup mean? | A tool for fixing bikes | A copy of the police report | *Extra help that joins in when needed | A plate of food for later
exercise: Which phrase means to support a friend? | Call a friend's backup | *Back someone up | Make a backup of a friend | Backup a friend's bike
test: Ollie's laptop was stolen, but his photos were safe. Why? | *He had a backup in another place | Photos cannot be lost at all | He had hidden the laptop under his bed | The thief gave the laptop back
test: In «Always have a backup plan ready», what does backup mean? | A traffic jam on the road | Extra players for the team | A copy of a photo | *Something ready in case the first plan fails
exam: Which sentence uses back up as a verb? | *Please back up your files before you wipe the laptop | The backup is kept in the cupboard | The backup power kept the lights on | Our backup plan was ready for the trip
